# Mafia – Backend

The backend runs on [Supabase](https://supabase.com): database, auth, realtime, and edge functions. All Supabase files live in `backend/supabase/`.

```
backend/
└── supabase/
    ├── config.toml      # project settings
    ├── migrations/      # SQL changes to the database (tables, security rules)
    └── functions/       # edge functions (game logic that runs on the server)
```

## First-time setup (project owner only)

1. Create a project at supabase.com and note its **project ref** and API keys.
2. In the terminal:
   ```bash
   cd backend
   npx supabase init
   npx supabase login
   npx supabase link --project-ref <your-project-ref>
   ```
3. Share the project URL and **anon** key with the team (they go in `frontend/.env`).

## Everyday commands (run from `backend/`)

```bash
npx supabase migration new <name>       # create a new SQL migration file
npx supabase functions new <name>       # create a new edge function
npx supabase db push                    # apply migrations to the project (owner only)
npx supabase functions deploy <name>    # deploy an edge function (owner only)
```

## Rules

- Change the database only through migration files, never by hand in the dashboard, so every change is reviewed in a PR.
- Never commit the service-role key or any secrets.
- Secret game logic (who has which role, night actions, vote results) is decided here on the server, never in the app.

## Git workflow

Nobody pushes directly to `main` or `dev`.

```bash
git checkout dev && git pull
git checkout -b feature/<short-name>
git push -u origin feature/<short-name>
```

Then open a pull request into `dev`. The project owner reviews and merges it.